{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25145654",
      "title": "Utilizing Incremental Static Generation (ISR)",
      "lectureOrder": 271,
      "videoOrder": 252,
      "sourceHash": "33ffc244134de6b021b7244825682cc7659d3c0983c1822f7a9ef2f72e8bab7f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 4.89,
          "en": "So we did learn about get static props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.89,
          "end": 8.6,
          "en": "and how we can use it to prepare data on the server side",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.6,
          "end": 12.12,
          "en": "so to say, for pre-rendering the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.12,
          "end": 14.328,
          "en": "However, when I say on the server side,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.328,
          "end": 16.259,
          "en": "that's only partially correct.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.259,
          "end": 20.19,
          "en": "We can execute server-side code here, but in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.19,
          "end": 23.46,
          "en": "the code will not run on the actual server, which serves",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.46,
          "end": 26.31,
          "en": "our application, instead it runs on our machine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.31,
          "end": 29.44,
          "en": "when the page is built when the application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.44,
          "end": 31.17,
          "en": "is built with next.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.17,
          "end": 34.86,
          "en": "So in the end, when you run, NPM run build.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.86,
          "end": 39.25,
          "en": "When you execute that prepared script here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.25,
          "end": 44.25,
          "en": "which executes next build, then this code is executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.86,
          "end": 49.23,
          "en": "Now that's still good because since we have no JS installed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.23,
          "end": 51.87,
          "en": "all that node JS code does work here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.87,
          "end": 56.14,
          "en": "So that's perfect, but it has one potential downside.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.14,
          "end": 61.03,
          "en": "What if you have data that changes frequently?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.03,
          "end": 65.63,
          "en": "Because I mean, pre-generating the pages sounds great",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.63,
          "end": 68.72,
          "en": "if you're building something fairly static.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 68.72,
          "end": 70.82,
          "en": "If you're building a blog, where data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.82,
          "end": 73.68,
          "en": "doesn't change too often, then of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 73.68,
          "end": 75.93,
          "en": "whenever you add a new blog post,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.93,
          "end": 78.529,
          "en": "you can just pre-generate your project again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.529,
          "end": 81.43,
          "en": "you can run NPM run build again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 81.43,
          "end": 84.14,
          "en": "and deploy the updated project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.14,
          "end": 85.81,
          "en": "So that would work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.81,
          "end": 89.49,
          "en": "But if you have data that changes more frequently,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.49,
          "end": 91.74,
          "en": "if we add a fourth product here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.74,
          "end": 95.451,
          "en": "after the page was deployed, then we have to rebuild",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.451,
          "end": 98.387,
          "en": "and redeploy the page all the time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.387,
          "end": 103.17,
          "en": "And that doesn't sound like a great thing to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 103.17,
          "end": 106.911,
          "en": "Well, Next.js also has solutions for this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 106.911,
          "end": 111.376,
          "en": "Solution number one is that you do pre-build your page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.376,
          "end": 115.46000000000001,
          "en": "but then you still include standard react code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.46000000000001,
          "end": 118.886,
          "en": "in your react components, where you use, use effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 118.886,
          "end": 123.38,
          "en": "for then fetching updated data from a server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 123.38,
          "end": 126.13,
          "en": "So you would always serve back a page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 126.13,
          "end": 128.648,
          "en": "with some pre-rendered data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 128.648,
          "end": 131.41,
          "en": "but that data might be outdated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 131.41,
          "end": 134.19,
          "en": "So you fetched a latest data in the background",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 134.19,
          "end": 139.19,
          "en": "and then update the loaded page after that data arrived.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 139.42000000000002,
          "end": 141.95,
          "en": "That's a pattern you could implement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 141.95,
          "end": 145.43,
          "en": "Then you at least chose something to your users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 145.43,
          "end": 147.57999999999998,
          "en": "but it might be a bit outdated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 147.57999999999998,
          "end": 149.938,
          "en": "but that's why you're fetching data in the background,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 149.938,
          "end": 152.3,
          "en": "so that you can update the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 152.3,
          "end": 155.28,
          "en": "with the latest data once you got that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 155.28,
          "end": 158.7,
          "en": "That might be a perfectly valid pattern,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 158.7,
          "end": 162.24,
          "en": "but there is an alternative which often is better.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 162.24,
          "end": 166.514,
          "en": "This get static props function, as I mentioned does execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 166.514,
          "end": 170.38,
          "en": "when you build your project with next build,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 170.38,
          "end": 172.65,
          "en": "so with this build script.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 172.65,
          "end": 174.62,
          "en": "Well, that's not entirely true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174.62,
          "end": 178.075,
          "en": "It does execute there, but that is not necessarily",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 178.075,
          "end": 181.3,
          "en": "the only time it executes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 181.3,
          "end": 184.2,
          "en": "Instead, Next.js has a built in feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.2,
          "end": 189.14,
          "en": "which is called incremental static generation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 189.14,
          "end": 191.37,
          "en": "It means that you don't just generate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 191.37,
          "end": 194.75,
          "en": "your page statically once at build time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 194.75,
          "end": 197.15,
          "en": "but that it's continuously updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 197.15,
          "end": 202.15,
          "en": "even after deployment without you re-deploying it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 202.37,
          "end": 205.63,
          "en": "So you pre-generate a page, but then you can also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 205.63,
          "end": 209.405,
          "en": "tell Next.js that a given page should be re-generated again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 209.405,
          "end": 214.405,
          "en": "for every incoming request at most every X seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 215.95,
          "end": 218.52,
          "en": "So every 60 seconds, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 218.52,
          "end": 221.195,
          "en": "That means that if a request is made",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 221.195,
          "end": 226.195,
          "en": "for a certain page and it's, let's say less than 60 seconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 226.82999999999998,
          "end": 230.41,
          "en": "since it was last re-generated, the existing page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 230.41,
          "end": 232.46,
          "en": "would be served to the visitor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 232.46,
          "end": 235.136,
          "en": "But if it's past those 60 seconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 235.136,
          "end": 238.35,
          "en": "and the amount of seconds of course is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 238.35,
          "end": 242.73,
          "en": "then this page would be pre-generated on the server instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 242.73,
          "end": 245.82,
          "en": "So that means that you either serve the old page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 245.82,
          "end": 249.868,
          "en": "if it's not that old yet, or you serve the latest page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 249.868,
          "end": 253.285,
          "en": "and brand new page, which was generated again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 253.285,
          "end": 256,
          "en": "on the server otherwise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 256,
          "end": 259.45,
          "en": "And if that page was pre-generated again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 259.45,
          "end": 262.03,
          "en": "on the server, because it was outdated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 262.03,
          "end": 264.16700000000003,
          "en": "then this newly generated page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 264.16700000000003,
          "end": 268.157,
          "en": "will replace the existing old page on the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 268.157,
          "end": 271.055,
          "en": "It will be cashed and future visitors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 271.055,
          "end": 275.29,
          "en": "will see that re-generated page instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 275.29,
          "end": 277.26,
          "en": "Until 60 seconds passed again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 277.26,
          "end": 280.38,
          "en": "and then new page is pre-generated again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 280.38,
          "end": 284.311,
          "en": "So you can have ongoing pre-rendering on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 284.311,
          "end": 287.75,
          "en": "for incoming requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 287.75,
          "end": 292.68,
          "en": "And all you need to do to unlock this is in the object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 292.68,
          "end": 295.13,
          "en": "which you return in get static props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 295.13,
          "end": 297.223,
          "en": "You don't just return props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 297.223,
          "end": 301.873,
          "en": "but you also add a second key, which is called revalidate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 302.83,
          "end": 305.81,
          "en": "And as a value, you set a number a year,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 305.81,
          "end": 309.101,
          "en": "which is the time in seconds that Next.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 309.101,
          "end": 313.27,
          "en": "should wait until it re-generates this page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 313.27,
          "end": 317.61,
          "en": "So for example, if I enter 10 here, we would tell Next.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 317.61,
          "end": 320.44,
          "en": "that for every incoming request to this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 320.44,
          "end": 323.94,
          "en": "it should be re-generated unless,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 323.94,
          "end": 328.94,
          "en": "it's less than 10 seconds ago that it was last re-generated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 329.14,
          "end": 333.266,
          "en": "So it's recreated at most once every 10 seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 333.266,
          "end": 336.53,
          "en": "And of course the higher this number is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 336.53,
          "end": 339.36,
          "en": "the less this page will be re-generated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 339.36,
          "end": 342.65,
          "en": "And it's totally up to you which value you want here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 342.65,
          "end": 345.082,
          "en": "It will of course depend on which kind of application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 345.082,
          "end": 347.18,
          "en": "you're building.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 347.18,
          "end": 350.635,
          "en": "For a highly dynamic page where content changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 350.635,
          "end": 353.439,
          "en": "all the time, you want a very low value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 353.439,
          "end": 356.11,
          "en": "maybe just one second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 356.11,
          "end": 359.483,
          "en": "For pages where the content is less dynamic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 359.483,
          "end": 362.95,
          "en": "maybe 10 minutes is enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 362.95,
          "end": 365.973,
          "en": "So that is then really something you have to decide.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 366.82,
          "end": 370.76,
          "en": "Now during development, the page will be re-generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 370.76,
          "end": 374.27,
          "en": "for every request, no matter what you enter here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 374.27,
          "end": 377.327,
          "en": "So with the development server, we will always see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 377.327,
          "end": 379.861,
          "en": "the latest page with the latest data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 379.861,
          "end": 382.42,
          "en": "and this will always run again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 382.42,
          "end": 385.46,
          "en": "But in production this number will matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 385.46,
          "end": 390.46,
          "en": "So here, if I add, re-generating here in a console log,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 395.14,
          "end": 399.42,
          "en": "instead of get static props, if I now rerun",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 399.42,
          "end": 404.23,
          "en": "the development server, we will see here in this terminal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 404.23,
          "end": 407.53,
          "en": "since that is server side terminal, so to say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 407.53,
          "end": 411.4,
          "en": "we see re-generating, because I started the Def server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 411.4,
          "end": 413.89,
          "en": "So that's equivalent to the build process.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 413.89,
          "end": 416.63,
          "en": "It was now pre-generated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 416.63,
          "end": 419.65,
          "en": "But if I now visit this page by reloading, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 419.65,
          "end": 422.286,
          "en": "we see this again, because as I just said,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 422.286,
          "end": 426.5,
          "en": "during development, the revalidate number doesn't matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 426.5,
          "end": 428.87,
          "en": "It will re-generate it every time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 428.87,
          "end": 430.54,
          "en": "In production it will matter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 430.54,
          "end": 433.28,
          "en": "and then you have the best of both worlds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 433.28,
          "end": 435.21,
          "en": "You have a pre-rendered page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 435.21,
          "end": 438.195,
          "en": "which then still is updated after deployment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 438.195,
          "end": 440.773,
          "en": "just as defined by you.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
